      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Big Lake sits at the western end of the Matanuska‑Susitna Valley, a region historically inhabited by the Dena’ina people of Cook Inlet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://biglakechamber.org/big-lake-history.html",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the 1950s, Big Lake had grown into a community featuring a quonset‑hut school, a gas station, a general store, a church, and marinas, lodges, and bars.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://biglakechamberak.org/visitor-info/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The North State Recreation Site on Big Lake covers 19 acres and offers a campground, picnic areas, a boat launch, and jetski rentals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Lake%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Big Lake receives an average of 51.4 inches of snowfall each year, enjoys 131 sunny days, and experiences an average wind speed of 8.18 mph.",
